WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.120
Speaker 1: Let's get to the most important
bag, which is the mailbag.

00:00:04.120 --> 00:00:07.270
You can email info at David Pakman dot com
on Fridays.

00:00:07.270 --> 00:00:10.430
We will feature some, but not nearly all.

00:00:10.430 --> 00:00:12.611
I mean, listen, we get thousands of messages
a week.

00:00:12.611 --> 00:00:16.470
We will feature some of the messages that
come in.

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:18.520
Info at David Pakman dot com compliments.

00:00:18.520 --> 00:00:19.520
Welcome.

00:00:19.520 --> 00:00:27.770
Of course, questions prioritized, criticisms
received, and then trolling more or less ignored.

00:00:27.770 --> 00:00:28.890
But not always.

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:31.789
Let's start with the first message.

00:00:31.789 --> 00:00:35.900
This one is from Ben and it is about George
Soros.

00:00:35.900 --> 00:00:39.150
Ben says, Hello, David.

00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:43.340
Is it true that you are being funded by George
Soros?

00:00:43.340 --> 00:00:51.040
I have heard that in South Korea, my country,
George Soros and an international Jewish cabal

00:00:51.040 --> 00:00:57.390
are trying to destroy the country by funding
mass immigration and low birthrates in order

00:00:57.390 --> 00:01:01.110
to achieve world domination.

00:01:01.110 --> 00:01:03.830
Is this true?

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:05.580
You know it's not true.

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:07.440
And there's a couple of things going on here.

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:10.290
First of all, George Soros is 92 years old.

00:01:10.290 --> 00:01:17.110
I think that at this point, even if at one
point he had his heart set on global domination,

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:21.060
domination through low birth rates and all
these different things that take decades,

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:22.630
if not longer to do.

00:01:22.630 --> 00:01:25.880
I think at this point, he's probably done
with that plan.

00:01:25.880 --> 00:01:27.600
He is now 92 years old.

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:33.050
And most importantly, no, I am not funded
by George Soros.

00:01:33.050 --> 00:01:38.800
Not funded by George Soros, not funded by
the DNC, not funded by whoever you think were

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:41.700
funded by and funded by people in the audience.

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:47.230
Probably not like Ben, but people in the audience
who value what we do and choose to support

00:01:47.230 --> 00:01:48.230
it.

00:01:48.230 --> 00:01:54.200
Paul wrote in and says, Your stated opinion
in past episodes on YouTube was that you were

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:59.380
doubtful Trump would ever be prosecuted for
the crimes he's committed in light of recent

00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:04.510
events at various court proceedings and particularly
the stealing of classified information.

00:02:04.510 --> 00:02:07.080
Have you now revised your opinion?

00:02:07.080 --> 00:02:08.080
Thank you.

00:02:08.080 --> 00:02:09.080
I have.

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:12.540
And as I've said before, I would love to be
wrong on this.

00:02:12.540 --> 00:02:19.200
I now believe that Donald Trump is likely
to be indicted and not likely to serve even

00:02:19.200 --> 00:02:21.700
a single day behind bars.

00:02:21.700 --> 00:02:23.660
That's my current opinion.

00:02:23.660 --> 00:02:28.730
And as many of you might know, if you watch
the show at all regularly, I revise my opinions

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:32.010
as information becomes available.

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:34.500
And I think that that's a great thing to do.

00:02:34.500 --> 00:02:37.000
It's something that should be encouraged.

00:02:37.000 --> 00:02:39.569
And I now believe Trump will be indicted.

00:02:39.569 --> 00:02:42.150
No prison time.

00:02:42.150 --> 00:02:45.020
Curious to hear from you, your thoughts.

00:02:45.020 --> 00:02:47.230
Paul wrote in about student loan forgiveness.

00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:54.230
Paul says, David, I know many see the student
loan relief as a good thing, but I see problems

00:02:54.230 --> 00:02:55.410
with it.

00:02:55.410 --> 00:02:59.410
I will say that I'm happy that it seems well
targeted.

00:02:59.410 --> 00:03:03.630
Only $10,000 to people earning under 125,000.

00:03:03.630 --> 00:03:06.930
My issue with it is that it's a Band-Aid and
it sets a precedent.

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:11.410
It may help people with debt now, but it won't
convince next year's students to think twice

00:03:11.410 --> 00:03:14.000
before taking out large loans that they can't
afford.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:15.520
And we'll be right back.

00:03:15.520 --> 00:03:19.660
In the same place, people will be clamoring
for another round of student loan relief in

00:03:19.660 --> 00:03:20.660
five years.

00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:23.980
Younger siblings will say, my older sister
got relief.

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:25.340
Now it's my turn.

00:03:25.340 --> 00:03:27.890
This can't become an ongoing expectation.

00:03:27.890 --> 00:03:33.069
Wouldn't this money be better spent trying
to make education more affordable for future

00:03:33.069 --> 00:03:37.580
and current students, rather than forgiving
loans for people who already agreed to pay

00:03:37.580 --> 00:03:39.860
them off for giving the interest?

00:03:39.860 --> 00:03:41.420
So the debt doesn't keep growing.

00:03:41.420 --> 00:03:45.940
But keeping the principle is also a great
idea that I've heard others mention.

00:03:45.940 --> 00:03:47.660
Curious to hear your thoughts.

00:03:47.660 --> 00:03:48.709
Good show.

00:03:48.709 --> 00:03:50.810
Yeah, I've addressed this.

00:03:50.810 --> 00:03:57.520
The student loan debt relief won't do anything
to put downward pressure on the price of college

00:03:57.520 --> 00:03:59.540
and university and higher education.

00:03:59.540 --> 00:04:00.540
And we need to do that.

00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:01.720
The system is broken.

00:04:01.720 --> 00:04:02.720
The system is broken.

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:04.690
I was calculating the other day.

00:04:04.690 --> 00:04:08.330
If prices continue increasing.

00:04:08.330 --> 00:04:10.410
Over the next eight years.

00:04:10.410 --> 00:04:17.430
By the time my daughter would go to college,
the college that my girlfriend went to would

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:18.959
cost $206,000 a year.

00:04:18.959 --> 00:04:19.959
All right.

00:04:19.959 --> 00:04:23.860
So you're talking like 850 K for four years.

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:27.180
Is that possible or does that sound like something's
broken?

00:04:27.180 --> 00:04:29.969
So absolutely something needs to change.

00:04:29.969 --> 00:04:33.879
And just a little a sprinkling of student
loan debt relief isn't going to do it.

00:04:33.879 --> 00:04:36.990
And so this is two different problems.

00:04:36.990 --> 00:04:37.990
It's one problem.

00:04:37.990 --> 00:04:39.300
The system is broken.

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:41.389
But there's two different parts to it.

00:04:41.389 --> 00:04:43.969
Existing debt and doing something about the
cost of college.

00:04:43.969 --> 00:04:47.629
What Joe Biden does does something about existing
debt.

00:04:47.629 --> 00:04:49.940
It doesn't deal with the cost of college.

00:04:49.940 --> 00:04:53.020
We need, at minimum, free community college.

00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:58.249
If tons of people who would go to a four year
school and take on four years of debt say,

00:04:58.249 --> 00:04:59.610
hey, you know what?

00:04:59.610 --> 00:05:04.139
I'll do my first two years for free at community
college if that happens.

00:05:04.139 --> 00:05:09.060
Demand for the four year schools will go down
and those schools will have to, if they want

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:12.310
to increase the number of people who are interested
and willing to go.

00:05:12.310 --> 00:05:14.789
They're going to have to decrease prices.

00:05:14.789 --> 00:05:15.999
That is one idea.

00:05:15.999 --> 00:05:18.180
And there's many others.

00:05:18.180 --> 00:05:22.500
Another idea which is controversial to some
is make it more difficult to get the loans.

00:05:22.500 --> 00:05:28.690
If it's more difficult to just get a loan
for 400 K to go wherever you want for whatever

00:05:28.690 --> 00:05:33.900
degree, if it becomes more difficult, that
would put downward pressure.

00:05:33.900 --> 00:05:36.139
So I'm with you 100%, Paul.

00:05:36.139 --> 00:05:39.229
This doesn't deal with the second issue.

00:05:39.229 --> 00:05:43.419
It only deals with the debt and we need to
be dealing with both.

00:05:43.419 --> 00:05:45.119
Clint wrote in about Hillary Clinton.

00:05:45.119 --> 00:05:47.080
I don't know what the hell Clint's talking
about here.

00:05:47.080 --> 00:05:48.849
