are positioning ourselves for Pete Buttigieg.

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:10.169
You can correct me if I'm wrong.

00:06:10.169 --> 00:06:13.770
If you're going to say anything about Hillary,
at least speak positive.

00:06:13.770 --> 00:06:18.569
Well, listen, Clint, I will sometimes say
positive things about Hillary and sometimes

00:06:18.569 --> 00:06:20.029
I will say negative things about Hillary.

00:06:20.029 --> 00:06:22.780
I will say whatever I want about Hillary on
the show.

00:06:22.780 --> 00:06:28.229
But in terms of she's not running and speak
poorly, I don't know what you're talking about,

00:06:28.229 --> 00:06:29.229
Clinton.

00:06:29.229 --> 00:06:30.389
I never said Hillary was running.

00:06:30.389 --> 00:06:36.610
I did do a story a couple of months ago indicating
that there are high level Democratic Party

00:06:36.610 --> 00:06:39.360
people talking about Hillary running again.

00:06:39.360 --> 00:06:43.680
I didn't say it was former, you know, lower
level staff or anything like that.

00:06:43.680 --> 00:06:45.960
But Clinton, maybe the message was meant for
someone else.

00:06:45.960 --> 00:06:47.520
I don't know.

00:06:47.520 --> 00:06:50.469
But we'll see if we can figure out about it.

00:06:50.469 --> 00:06:53.879
Chris wrote in and asked, Is losing better?

00:06:53.879 --> 00:07:01.179
David, do you think it may be becoming a Republican
strategy to lose just enough elections to

00:07:01.179 --> 00:07:05.889
not have a majority power in the Senate, but
still have enough seats to filibuster major

00:07:05.889 --> 00:07:06.949
legislation?

00:07:06.949 --> 00:07:09.399
And this could apply to the White House in
2024 as well.

00:07:09.399 --> 00:07:14.559
My point is they seem to enjoy being able
to criticize everything Democrats do, and

00:07:14.559 --> 00:07:17.360
they don't really have any policies to speak
of.

00:07:17.360 --> 00:07:22.599
Mitch McConnell always talks about his main
objective is to win elections, but maybe not.

00:07:22.599 --> 00:07:23.599
What do you think?

00:07:23.599 --> 00:07:31.129
Well, I've addressed this in a very specific
way, which is Republicans in 2024 want to

00:07:31.129 --> 00:07:36.479
make the case that Biden should be replaced
with a Republican because he didn't get anything

00:07:36.479 --> 00:07:37.669
done.

00:07:37.669 --> 00:07:44.189
And so Republicans want to ensure that Biden
and Democrats don't get anything done.

00:07:44.189 --> 00:07:49.479
And a great way to do that is to have divided
Congress, Democrats controlling the Senate

00:07:49.479 --> 00:07:51.219
and Republicans controlling the House.

00:07:51.219 --> 00:07:57.159
It's a great way for in the lead up to the
24 election, Republicans to be able to say,

00:07:57.159 --> 00:08:00.110
look, they've had the White House for four
years.

00:08:00.110 --> 00:08:02.429
They've had the Senate for four years.

00:08:02.429 --> 00:08:04.479
And when's the last time they got anything
done?

00:08:04.479 --> 00:08:09.199
And of course, there would be that two year
stretch where nothing gets done because Republicans

00:08:09.199 --> 00:08:10.869
control the House.

00:08:10.869 --> 00:08:17.300
So I don't know about the bigger picture,
Chris, of just never get anything done.

00:08:17.300 --> 00:08:22.490
But I think in the immediate, that's exactly
their goal with Joe Biden and Democrats over

00:08:22.490 --> 00:08:24.830
the next two years.

00:08:24.830 --> 00:08:30.520
Terry wrote in and said, You messaged me and
I'm going to keep doing this for as long as

00:08:30.520 --> 00:08:31.520
I have to.

00:08:31.520 --> 00:08:36.770
Terry said, David, I was watching your YouTube
show last night and I got two messages that

00:08:36.770 --> 00:08:38.220
